  "title": "A complementary dataset of open-eyes EEG recordings in a photo-stimulation setting from: Alzheimer's disease, Frontotemporal dementia and Healthy subjects",
  "description": "This dataset provides eyes-open scalp EEG recordings acquired during intermittent photic stimulation (5 to 30 Hz in 5 Hz steps) from 36 participants with Alzheimer's disease, 23 with frontotemporal dementia, and 29 healthy controls. It complements an earlier eyes-closed resting-state dataset of the same cohort, and participant numbers match between the two. Raw and preprocessed (filtered, ASR- and ICA-cleaned) recordings are provided in BIDS format alongside clinical MMSE scores and demographics.",
  "methods_description": "Recordings were made at the 2nd Department of Neurology of AHEPA General Hospital, Thessaloniki, with a Nihon Kohden EEG 2100 clinical device. Nineteen scalp electrodes were placed according to the 10-20 system, with A1/A2 mastoid electrodes, at a 500 Hz sampling rate, with impedance kept below 5 kOhm and Cz as the common reference. Preprocessing applied a 0.5-45 Hz Butterworth band-pass filter, re-referencing to A1-A2, Artifact Subspace Reconstruction, and ICA with ICLabel-based automatic rejection of eye and jaw components.",
